From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 06:36:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip: qcom-pdc: report the selected X1E mode

The X1E PDC v4 backport either selects pass-through mode through SCM or
falls back to supporting firmware-configured secondary-controller mode.
Report which path the retail Surface firmware takes so suspend results
can be interpreted.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/irqchip/qcom-pdc.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/qcom-pdc.c b/drivers/irqchip/qcom-pdc.c
index ce6d80c7f17a..97835e1542e7 100644
--- a/drivers/irqchip/qcom-pdc.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/qcom-pdc.c
@@ -724,6 +724,11 @@ static int qcom_pdc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev, struct device_node *pare
 			pdc->mode = PDC_SECONDARY_MODE;
 			pdc->unmask_gpio = pdc_unmask_gpio_cfg;
 			pdc->clear_gpio = pdc_clear_gpio_cfg;
+			dev_warn(dev,
+				 "SCM could not select PDC pass-through mode (%d); using secondary-controller mode\n",
+				 ret);
+		} else {
+			dev_info(dev, "PDC pass-through mode selected through SCM\n");
 		}
 	}
 
